note Text as the tree and the canvas carry it. A Label is an owned string measured in columns: one per character, two per icon glyph (see icons), because one monospace font makes a width a count. A Run is a Label in one colour, and a Text element is a vector of runs at one font size, either on one line or wrapped at words to the element's width (only the first run's text and colour are used when wrapping). A Grid is a block of cells, each a glyph and a colour, built once per view and shared by Rc into the draw list, which is how a whole file of highlighted code is drawn without a text run per token.

